The product of three different positive integers is equal to \(7^3 = 343\). To find three distinct positive integers whose product is 343, we can express 343 as the product of its prime factors. Since 343 is \(7 \times 7 \times 7\), the only possible distinct positive integers are 1, 7, and 49. Thus, the sum of these integers is \(1 + 7 + 49 = 57\).

Answer: \boxed{57}

