To find the area Sandy needs to paint, follow these steps:

1. Determine the total area of the wall:
   \[
   \text{Total Area} = \text{Height} \times \text{Length} = 9 \, \text{ft} \times 12 \, \text{ft} = 108 \, \text{sq ft}
   \]

2. Calculate the area Sandy will not paint (the window):
   \[
   \text{Window Area} = 2 \, \text{ft} \times 4 \, \text{ft} = 8 \, \text{sq ft}
   \]

3. Subtract the window area from the total wall area to find the paintable area:
   \[
   \text{Paint Area} = \text{Total Area} - \text{Window Area} = 108 \, \text{sq ft} - 8 \, \text{sq ft} = 100 \, \text{sq ft}
   \]

**Answer:** \boxed{100}

