To find the greatest integer \( x \) such that \( \frac{7}{9} > \frac{x}{13} \), we can start by comparing the two fractions. Cross-multiplying gives \( 7 \times 13 > 9x \) → \( 91 > 9x \). Dividing both sides by 9 gives \( x < \frac{91}{9} ≈ 10.111 \). The greatest integer less than 10.111 is \( 10 \).

